# Security review

No vulnerabilities found. The identification pass returned NO FINDINGS:

- Generated scripts: both Gradle init scripts are fixed text written with
  printf; repo values reach the lint script only through BOOTSTRAP_LINT_MODULES
  and BOOTSTRAP_LINT_TASK (System.getenv, tokenize), never into the code.
- Shell inputs: SDK levels must match ^[0-9]+(\.[0-9]+)?$ before
  `android sdk install`; file lists from `git ls-files -z` and `find` are read
  NUL-safe or line by line, quoted, and never run. The eval of usage_files
  predates the branch; its input is a CLI flag.
- Temp files: mktemp -d with an EXIT trap; the kotlin task no longer copies or
  restores lockfiles.
- Paths: module folders are made canonical inside Gradle only to look up
  projects of a running build. The ANDROID_HOME check only tests existence.
- Swift: reorders checks and adds a `swift --version` probe; no new input.
